  message: "P2 REVIEW 2026-09-25 (dev e4a47383ab). LIKELY FIXED; NOT PROVEN. Status unchanged.\n\nThe filed failure is the JavaScript `dataflow_capable` False under co-resident full-suite ordering, in test_taint_recall_corpus.py (test_adjudication_label_does_not_depend_on_another_language / test_published_scope_distinguishes_capable_from_incapable). It matches the mechanism fixed in `dataflow_scope.ensure_def_use_extractors_registered`:\n- 4dcd87c0bf (2026-08-10) replaced the bare re-import with a reload plus a SUBSET check. Its comment names this exact symptom: test_py_def_use.py clears the registry and reloads only its own module, \"leaving it populated but missing javascript ... exactly how a full-suite run produced two JavaScript data-flow failures that every smaller scope passed\".\n- f013cc7d13 (2026-09-19, INV-zunik) makes the health baseline one the function produced itself, not whatever was registered first.\n\nWHY NOT CLOSED: the row itself records that CI never surfaced this (green at the failing commit). So the green cron full-suite at 615471e2 is not evidence. The close repro is the row's own local `-n 5` full multi-package run, twice. This review did not run pytest (forbidden in this pass), so the repro has not been re-run."  # 112f
- op: discuss  # 0237
  at: '2026-10-01T00:58:15Z'  # 0237
  by: agent  # 0237
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 0237
  clock: 3  # 0237
  nonce: '0237'  # 0237
  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-09-30 (dev 7f0f993843): PARTLY-DONE. The filed instance's mechanism was found and fixed the day after filing; the row's own HYPOTHESIS was not the mechanism; one analogue remains open on INV-votoj.\n- Real mechanism (not test_ddg_build's _preserve_registry): the DEF/USE registry, cleared by test_cfg.py (clear_def_use_extractors x5) and partially restored by test_py_def_use.py (reloads only its own module), so a bare re-import left javascript's extractor gone. Fixed in 4dcd87c0bf (2026-08-10): reload + subset check against a learned baseline. Commit body records a full suite of 22,255 passed / 0 failed against 2 failed before (that run's -n worker count is not stated). f013cc7d13 (2026-09-19, INV-zunik) makes the first call reload unconditionally so the baseline cannot be clipped. Code: dataflow_scope.py:311-375.\n- The row never links INV-votoj (status violated), which records this exact diagnosis and the residual.\n- RESIDUAL, read in code: the guard checks only cfg.registered_def_use_languages(). dataflow_capable also needs ddg_spec (dataflow_scope.py:400/412, ddg_build._DDG_LANGUAGES), and that registry is never compared against a baseline. A loss of javascript's DDG spec with its def/use extractor intact would not trigger a reload. The only test-side mutator of _DDG_LANGUAGES is test_ddg_build.py:32-39 (_preserve_registry) plus :71 (clear_ddg_languages, inside the fixture). I found no test in that file whose body first-imports ts_def_use, so I did NOT find a live path to the residual -- read only, not run.\n- Assertion moved: test_taint_recall_corpus.py:695 (was :687).\n- NOT RUN (forbidden in this pass): the row's own repro. What would confirm the filed instance closed: the row's 7-package `-n 5` local run on current dev, twice, 0 failures in test_taint_recall_corpus.py. A pass does not close the residual.\nPROPOSED: link INV-votoj; reword \"WHAT IS NOT ESTABLISHED -- the mechanism\" to cite 4dcd87c0bf/f013cc7d13; after the repro passes, close on the filed instance and leave the _DDG_LANGUAGES half on INV-votoj (item 1 of its unclosed list)."  # 0237
